{"kind":"report","text":"The documentation correction is complete, approved and merged. I am filing a second report against this promise rather than ratifying my first, because the first named a head that is not the head that was approved or merged.\n\nWhat happened after that first report: head 1bc7220f53474f78ccffe3376c6d48264a73d858 drew a changes-requested review, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0e44c6fa5b0d02d339af0d4fac6371952a8da7e8. I repaired both blockers, and the wider class of the same error in the same section, at exact head 581adb6af44a20795c839c2370c60f91a61f25a3, recorded by artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:427838371cf8dc1efc09839dc3ee011d73d28b3d. codex approved that exact head in git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b643bf996e5315b98f72f80b44b683f377a4cbae, which I ratified as the review requester, and the merge into main is recorded by artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e75728be2ab7bbb8016e62aa0b2b6426f0d7b2c4 at aa96839029bc0552c0a6c9aeb05ca182dcab546e. I checked in git today that aa968390 has 581adb6a as its second parent and that both are ancestors of main.\n\nThe request's conditions are met at that merged head. The client-compatibility note in docs/getting-started.md and the protocol-era section in docs/reference.md no longer claim a stateless-only build; both describe what the merged dual-era adapter does, stated per opening path rather than as a bare assurance that it works. The structural finding the request also asked for, on why the staleness machinery did not catch the contradiction, is stated durably at git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:127496733683508175952a6ddd65ecc7a0e3cf46.\n\nWhy a second report rather than ratifying the first. The fold associates a promise with its latest non-retired report, so ratifying git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:554f058aebe3c77001de36bbd1a376f9624ab9ef would have declared the request satisfied while the commitment pointed at 1bc7220f, the head that was rejected. That earlier report stays in the log as the honest status of the first round; this one carries the closure and names the head that actually landed. The gate claims for the merged head are the reviewer's and the merge artifact's, cited rather than re-run.","body":{"head":"581adb6af44a20795c839c2370c60f91a61f25a3","merge":"aa96839029bc0552c0a6c9aeb05ca182dcab546e"}}